Z||000005||Fierokid87||08-23-2001||01:28 AM||||Ok here is something for everyone with 87 V-6 Fieros.  I was wondering if the 87 V6 engine mount is the same as the 4 cyld.  Cuzz Im doing a swap from a 4 to a V6.  and when I went to try to test fit the solid mount for the V-6  to the cradle it did not fit.  please tell me what mount I need.  and if its the solid mount then do I drill new holes for is?<P>Thanks<BR>Scott<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fieroguy1987<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierokid87||08-23-2001||01:52 AM||||bump<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fieroguy1987<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Neal||08-23-2001||02:04 AM||||mounts are simple to change.  Get a jack, jackstands, a short 2X4, and the proper wrenches (i think its a 15mm)<P>Now im a V6 owner so i cant vouch for the engine mount on the 4cyl, but the tranny mounts are the same, and if you are unsure of the dogbone just take it to a shop.<P>jack up car<BR>place jackstands<BR>break loose all mount bolts/nuts<BR>place 2X4 on jack and under under oil pan<BR>lift till it is resting on the oil pan.<BR>remove nuts for engine mount<BR>jack up engine remove mount<BR>install new mount.<P>very similar for the tranny mounts, just place jack and 2X4 under tranny.<P><BR>FIEROKID:  the 87 v6 uses a rubber mount that is about inline with the strut.  it is mounted to the engine with an L shaped bracket and mounts to the cradle by a metal tab that is welded onto the insde.<BR>hope that helps||||reg||1
Z||000008||starfighter007@msn.com||08-23-2001||01:13 PM||||That seems simple enough thank you Neal.||||reg||14
